# The offline stack needs NO configuration. `pytest`, `python -m router.gate`
# and `python scripts/run_demo.py` all run with no key and no network.
#
# This file exists only for scripts/real_run.py, the paid capture, which
# measures three things the offline stack cannot: whether a real embedding model
# reclaims the paraphrase queries its bag-of-tokens stand-in loses, how an LLM
# router compares with the deterministic heuristic one, and how much either
# answer moves when you ask again.
#
#   ENV_FILE=~/.secrets/ai.env python scripts/real_run.py
#
# Keys live in a private file outside this repository and are loaded by path,
# so no key ever appears in a command line or a transcript.

# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# text-embedding-3-small at 1536 dimensions is the default. The offline mock is
# 256; the width difference is itself part of what the capture measures.
# OPENAI_EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.6-terra
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Independent routing passes per router. 5 is the default and the value the
# capture in SAMPLE_RUN.md was taken at. Cost scales linearly with it: each run
# is one completion per query per configured model, so 5 runs x 19 queries x 2
# models is 190 calls. The embedding half does NOT scale with it -- the corpus
# is embedded twice regardless, once per pass of the reproducibility check.
# STABILITY_RUNS=5
